00:11:27.985 --> 00:11:29.404
in Twitter and Facebook and a lot of

00:11:29.404 --> 00:11:31.044
crazy things started happening,

00:11:31.044 --> 00:11:34.282
and now I run a very
large social media agency,

00:11:34.282 --> 00:11:35.367
800 people.

00:11:35.367 --> 00:11:38.394
But the family still owns the business.

00:11:38.394 --> 00:11:40.462
- Okay, why you don't do any more videos?

00:11:40.462 --> 00:11:41.448
- I haven't done videos.

00:11:41.448 --> 00:11:42.960
You know, five years every day.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.050
- (laughs) It's a lot.

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.128
- It was a run.

00:11:47.128 --> 00:11:48.473
- Awesome, nice to meet you buddy.

00:11:48.473 --> 00:11:49.484
- Thank you.

00:11:49.484 --> 00:11:51.676
Thank you for recognizing
me and thanks for watching.

00:11:51.676 --> 00:11:53.787
- That's awesome, it's a great show.

00:11:53.787 --> 00:11:54.620
- Thank you.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:55.453
- This one over here.

00:11:55.453 --> 00:11:56.286
- Thank you.

00:11:56.286 --> 00:11:57.119
Hello.

00:11:57.119 --> 00:11:57.952
- [Table] Hello!

00:11:57.952 --> 00:11:58.785
- [Gordon] I'm Gordon.

00:11:58.785 --> 00:12:00.178
- [Gary] Gordon, how are you, Gary.

00:12:00.178 --> 00:12:01.171
- [Gordon] Nice to meet you.

00:12:01.171 --> 00:12:02.295
- Hey, nice to meet you, Jason.

00:12:02.295 --> 00:12:03.292
- Jason, such a pleasure.

00:12:03.292 --> 00:12:04.312
- [Lady In Black] Gary, it's not your

00:12:04.312 --> 00:12:05.145
first time in Hong Kong?

00:12:05.145 --> 00:12:05.978
- It's my first time.

00:12:05.978 --> 00:12:08.569
No, it's even better, it's
my first time in Asia.

00:12:08.569 --> 00:12:09.720
- [Table] Oh!

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.720
- Oh, is it?

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:12.168
- [Blonde Lady] And not the last one, no?

00:12:12.168 --> 00:12:13.146
- No, not at all.

00:12:13.146 --> 00:12:16.402
Yeah, you know, a mix of serendipity

00:12:16.402 --> 00:12:19.754
and just focusing on the proper timing

00:12:19.754 --> 00:12:22.320
and making every second count,

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.840
I've been really looking forward to it,

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.011
and it's been, it's been so pent up

00:12:27.011 --> 00:12:30.731
that when we landed, in baggage claim,

00:12:30.731 --> 00:12:32.452
we weren't even out of baggage claim

00:12:32.452 --> 00:12:34.485
and I looked at D Rock, this is,

00:12:34.485 --> 00:12:36.030
I'm gonna like this place.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:37.446
(group laughs)

00:12:37.446 --> 00:12:40.253
It's been such a remarkable
two and a half days,

00:12:40.253 --> 00:12:42.305
like I can't wait to come back.

00:12:42.305 --> 00:12:44.831
The level of gratitude
for entrepreneurship

00:12:44.831 --> 00:12:46.648
and what it's done for me and my family,

00:12:46.648 --> 00:12:49.231
the energy in this marketplace,

00:12:51.185 --> 00:12:53.039
and in this region in general

00:12:53.039 --> 00:12:56.344
I think I associate more
a little bit even more

00:12:56.344 --> 00:12:59.604
than I would say than I
would associate with the US,

00:12:59.604 --> 00:13:02.237
and definitely Europe's version of it.

00:13:02.237 --> 00:13:03.487
So, that, yeah.

00:13:05.326 --> 00:13:06.484
I mean, I grew up in the wine business,

00:13:06.484 --> 00:13:08.876
I've spent a lot of time in Europe.

00:13:08.876 --> 00:13:12.293
The rawness to the entrepreneurial spirit

00:13:14.928 --> 00:13:16.845
is intoxicating for me.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:18.593
And so,

00:13:20.853 --> 00:13:22.254
I would say that's probably a thing

00:13:22.254 --> 00:13:24.831
that stood out the most.

00:13:24.831 --> 00:13:26.282
And I'll tell you another thing,

00:13:26.282 --> 00:13:29.032
and, I am quite passionate around

00:13:31.228 --> 00:13:34.311
having really important conversations

00:13:34.311 --> 00:13:38.419
with young entrepreneurs
around family dynamics.

00:13:38.419 --> 00:13:41.237
And I think one of the things I'm

00:13:41.237 --> 00:13:43.395
most excited about, obviously so much

00:13:43.395 --> 00:13:45.044
of my strategy in coming to Asia

00:13:45.044 --> 00:13:47.265
is leading with my content first.

00:13:47.265 --> 00:13:48.514
I think I'm gonna be able to help

00:13:48.514 --> 00:13:50.927
a lot of kids have difficult conversations

00:13:50.927 --> 00:13:53.205
with their parents that in a 50 year macro

00:13:53.205 --> 00:13:55.826
will be enormously beneficial,

00:13:55.826 --> 00:13:58.047
but because there's a lot of pressure

00:13:58.047 --> 00:14:02.098
in the Asian ecosystem around education

00:14:02.098 --> 00:14:03.675
or doing the right thing,

00:14:03.675 --> 00:14:06.568
and I'm very empathetic to that.

00:14:06.568 --> 00:14:08.818
My great moment of my life,

00:14:10.752 --> 00:14:12.171
I would actually argue is

00:14:12.171 --> 00:14:14.329
the fact that even
though I was an immigrant

00:14:14.329 --> 00:14:16.365
in the US my mom had enough self-esteem

00:14:16.365 --> 00:14:19.198
to support me being a bad student,

00:14:20.178 --> 00:14:24.449
which became the foundation of my success.

00:14:24.449 --> 00:14:25.992
- [Blonde Lady] Unconditional love.

00:14:25.992 --> 00:14:27.019
- Unconditional love,

00:14:27.019 --> 00:14:30.150
and really predicated on
enormous self-confidence

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:33.334
in my mom that she knew what
she was doing parenting,

00:14:33.334 --> 00:14:36.077
and didn't need to follow the blueprint.

00:14:36.077 --> 00:14:38.448
'Cause a lot of this has
to do with insecurities

00:14:38.448 --> 00:14:39.698
of the parents.

00:14:41.858 --> 00:14:46.348
So yeah, some interesting
things I picked up on already.

00:14:46.348 --> 00:14:49.448
- When you say the rawness,
what do you mean by that?

00:14:49.448 --> 00:14:52.095
- I think a little bit of a level of

00:14:52.095 --> 00:14:54.095
a chip on your shoulder,

00:14:58.335 --> 00:15:01.774
great wild wild west
slam grab opportunity,

00:15:01.774 --> 00:15:04.524
maybe even an inch or two of like

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:07.483
doing it at all costs.

00:15:09.557 --> 00:15:13.224
A little less polish,
a little less process.

00:15:14.522 --> 00:15:15.939
Results-oriented.

00:15:17.218 --> 00:15:19.435
One of the things that was fearful

00:15:19.435 --> 00:15:22.826
is an admiration of
Silicon Valley culture,

00:15:22.826 --> 00:15:26.511
which I think over time is
a negative for the region.

00:15:26.511 --> 00:15:28.654
Because then you start building financial

00:15:28.654 --> 00:15:31.738
arbitrage machines, not actual businesses.

00:15:31.738 --> 00:15:34.821
So yeah, just a little bit more of a,

00:15:35.766 --> 00:15:37.783
like just generally a little bit more

00:15:37.783 --> 00:15:39.450
of a go-to attitude.

00:15:42.587 --> 00:15:46.479
Yeah, like the questions, the tonality,

00:15:46.479 --> 00:15:48.094
even the way I'm being pitched.

00:15:48.094 --> 00:15:49.732
And you know what's interesting?

00:15:49.732 --> 00:15:52.152
What I'm trying to figure out is

00:15:52.152 --> 00:15:54.735
is there a chip on the shoulder

00:15:55.569 --> 00:15:58.730
to a US Silicon Valley-centric thing,

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.854
which I think there should be

00:16:00.854 --> 00:16:03.794
in a place where, especially when you look

00:16:03.794 --> 00:16:06.397
at mainland China, you
know, those companies,

00:16:06.397 --> 00:16:09.902
they're so much further
ahead in a lot of ways

00:16:09.902 --> 00:16:13.071
because of their full integration.

00:16:13.071 --> 00:16:14.581
I don't know, there's just,

00:16:14.581 --> 00:16:16.762
there's a clearly different tone,

00:16:16.762 --> 00:16:19.717
which my early intuition leads to

00:16:19.717 --> 00:16:22.884
good, with my other intuition which is

00:16:24.756 --> 00:16:27.783
there's too much looking at other places,

00:16:27.783 --> 00:16:30.152
and it should get, I think Asia should

00:16:30.152 --> 00:16:32.720
get more insular, 'cause
I think the natural

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.759
behaviors are better.

00:16:34.759 --> 00:16:35.820
- Right, right.

